{
  "configuration_id": "config_019",
  "reason": "The largest performance jump in the history is from singleprofile to multiprofile (0.537 → 0.725 with scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted). The critical uncertainty is whether this multiprofile gain is driven primarily by the RNA modality, the image modality, or their interaction. config_019 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, transformer) is a clean single-variable ablation of config_001: it removes only the image modality while keeping the RNA encoder, profile setting, and aggregation identical. If config_019 approaches ~0.70, the image contributes little and future effort should focus on RNA encoder/aggregation; if it drops substantially (e.g., to ~0.55–0.60), the image modality is a meaningful contributor in the multiprofile setting and image encoder selection becomes a priority. This is the highest-information experiment under the limited budget because it directly partitions the multiprofile gain between the two modalities and will determine where to invest remaining experiments."
}

